.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-record-nonverdict 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-record\-nonverdict \- Record which recent required\-check failures never reached a verdict
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten record nonverdict\fR [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-required\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\-job\fR] [\fB\-\-verdict\-step\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record which recent required\-check failures never reached a verdict
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<window>\fR
How many recent failed runs to read, 1 to 100 (default: 30)
.TP
\fB\-\-required\-check\fR \fI<required_check>\fR
A required job, by exact name; only these are counted (repeatable; default: $CI_REQUIRED_CHECKS)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-job\fR \fI<exclude_job>\fR
A job never counted, such as a fan\-in whose failure its siblings cause (repeatable; default: $CI_FANIN_CHECK)
.TP
\fB\-\-verdict\-step\fR \fI<verdict_step>\fR
A step\-name prefix that marks a failed step as verdict\-bearing (repeatable; default: $CI_VERDICT_STEPS)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
